Text: 5.1. Data augmentation The easiest and most common method to reduce overfitting on image data is to artificially enlarge the dataset using label- preserving transformations (e.g., Refs.4, 5, 30). We employ two distinct forms of data augmentation, both of which allow transformed images to be produced from the original images with very little computation, so the transformed images do not need to be stored on disk.

